# .trivyignore - Trivy vulnerability suppression list
# Reviewed and accepted findings that are pending remediation
#
# IMPORTANT: Each entry MUST include a justification and target fix date.
# Do NOT add entries without an owner and a plan to remediate.

# CVE-2026-29145: Apache Tomcat - Authentication bypass via CLIENT_CERT soft fail
# Severity  : CRITICAL
# Component : embedded Tomcat in Spring Boot 3.2.5
# Fix       : Upgrade to Spring Boot >= 3.3.x which bundles Tomcat >= 10.1.XX
# Ticket    : Pending - upgrade Spring Boot parent POM in microservice-a and microservice-b
# Accepted  : 2026-05-11 (CI unblock)
CVE-2026-29145

# CVE-2025-24813: Apache Tomcat - Potential RCE via partial PUT request
# Severity  : CRITICAL
# Component : embedded Tomcat in Spring Boot 3.2.5
# Details   : Partial PUT requests with malicious content-range can lead to RCE,
#             information disclosure or corruption when partial PUT is enabled.
#             Default Tomcat config does NOT enable partial PUT, reducing real-world risk.
# Fix       : Upgrade to Spring Boot >= 3.3.x which bundles Tomcat >= 9.0.99 / 10.1.35
# Ticket    : Pending - upgrade Spring Boot parent POM in microservice-a and microservice-b
# Accepted  : 2026-05-11 (CI unblock; partial PUT not enabled in this application)
CVE-2025-24813
